# Take School Focus twice, then cast an illusion and read the disbelief DC.
# (bd inc-q1ei)
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/school-focus.keys 42
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. The feat files its school in the stati's Mag
# (src/Create.cpp), and two of the three places that read it looked elsewhere:
# the duplicate guard in the menu below asked HasEffStati, which matches a
# RESOURCE ID against eID, and the disbelief save asked HasStati, which matches
# its second argument against Val. Both are 0 for this feat, so the menu
# offered a school the character already held and the illusionist's +2 never
# applied.
#
# WHY A MAGE. School Focus is FF_WIZARD and needs caster level 1, so only a
# spellcasting class is offered it at first level. The orc mage is the one
# tools/keys/chargen-mage.keys makes, on the same seed, so the race, subrace,
# class, attribute and alignment letters are that file's and can be compared
# against it when a menu moves.
#
# WHY PHANTASMAL FORCE. It is the only first-level illusion a mage can have
# that reaches the disbelief save at all: its 'f' branch
# (src/Effects.cpp) redirects a real attack spell at the victim with
# effIllusion set, and src/Magic.cpp then rolls the victim's Will save. The
# printed "Will Save: ... vs DC n" line is the oracle, and it is the only place
# a player can read that DC.
#
# WHY A GOBLIN. The disbelief save is skipped outright for a victim that is
# mindless, has true sight, or has scent, blindsight, tremorsense or sharpened
# senses (src/Magic.cpp). A goblin has none of them, and it stands where the
# summon puts it, one square east, so a single RIGHT reaches it in the
# targeting prompt.
#
# Every choice here is a menu letter, and menu letters move when the list
# changes. Run with the seed and the settings named above or the attribute
# rolls change, the offered feats change with them, and these letters choose
# something else.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
i       # Race:     [i] Orc
a       # Subrace:  [a] Orc (Standard)
d       # Class:    [d] Mage
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
e       # Alignment: [e] Neutral

# Wizard specialty: Illusion, and not the Evocation the other chargen scripts
# take. A specialist casts his own school at 100% and every other school at a
# penalty ("Lacking aptitude for Illusion, you find casting Phantasmal Force
# draining" was this script's first run), and a cast that fails to go off rolls
# no disbelief save at all. This is the only way to make the cast certain.
@expect "schools of magic"
@choose "Illusion"

# The feat list runs to 81 entries over two pages, and School Focus is on the
# second, so TAB comes before the name.
@expect "Choose a feat"
TAB
@choose "School Focus"
@expect "Choose a focus school:"
@dump:school-menu-1
@choose "Illusion"

# The second pick is the whole point: the school just taken must be gone.
@expect "Choose a feat"
TAB
@choose "School Focus"
@expect "Choose a focus school:"
@dump:school-menu-2
@choose "Evocation"

# Skill Manager. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected skill and stops at the
# skill's maximum, DOWN moves to the next, so three RIGHTs per skill spends
# everything available without needing to know how many ranks this character
# has. Character generation will not let go until the pool is empty. This is
# tools/keys/chargen-mage.keys's pass, written out rather than looped: a mage
# is offered exactly one Skill Manager, and a second @while aimed at a screen
# that is no longer there spends its keys on the menus that follow.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

@while "wish to worship" y
@expect "personality archetype"
a       # Personality archetype

# The starting spells. An Illusion specialist is granted Phantasmal Force
# outright -- it is the one first-level illusion the offered list does NOT
# carry -- so these picks are whatever the list opens on, and the cast below
# is what proves the spell is really known.
@expect "Learn which spell"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@until "Things in View" ESC

# The character sheet's feat list, as evidence that both schools are really on
# him and that the second pick was not thrown away.
d
@until "School Focus" DOWN
@dump:sheet
@until "Things in View" ESC

# 'w' opens wizard mode and 'y' confirms it the first time. The pair is driven
# by @until rather than written out, because a keystroke swallowed by a prompt
# that was still up would spend every key after it on the wrong thing.
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w y
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
# The switch list draws no cursor a screen dump can see, so this counts rows:
# Freeze Monsters is the eleventh, and the cursor opens on the first.
DOWN*10
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:summoned

m
@choose "Phantasmal Force"
f       # Create illusionary creature, item, trap or force? -- force
@choose "Magic Missile"
RIGHT   # the targeting cursor, one square east, onto the goblin
@expect "A goblin"
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE

# The roll line scrolls off the top line as soon as anything else prints, so
# the message history is where it is read.
v
@dump:disbelief
